{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"fa13a0b059b6cc15ea0184e6bffa041dc3999073f682fea752e128e37bd6c29e","slug":"linux-intro","location":"/introduction/linux_intro.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Linux Introduction","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Kevin Goebbert","given":"Kevin","family":"Goebbert"},"name":"Kevin Goebbert","affiliations":["University of Tampa"],"id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"license":{"content":{"id":"CC-BY-4.0","url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","note":"All non-code content is licensed under CC-BY-4.0","free":true,"CC":true},"code":{"id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://opensource.org/licenses/Apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","note":"All code content is licensed under Apache-2.0","free":true,"osi":true}},"github":"https://github.com/kgoebber/metpy_thebook","edit_url":null,"numbering":{"title":{"enabled":false,"offset":1},"equation":{"enabled":false},"figure":{"enabled":true,"continue":true}},"keywords":["metpy","python","meteorology","weather"],"copyright":"2026","affiliations":[{"id":"University of Tampa","name":"University of Tampa"}],"settings":{"output_stderr":"remove-warn","output_matplotlib_strings":"remove"},"source_url":"https://github.com/kgoebber/metpy_thebook/blob/main/introduction/linux_intro.md","thumbnail":"/metpy_thebook/_public/launch_terminal_wind-68b996fdcf44a009f36b386a7f937206.png","thumbnailOptimized":"/metpy_thebook/_public/launch_terminal_wind-68b996fdcf44a009f36b386a7f937206.webp","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"linux_intro.md","url":"/metpy_thebook/_public/linux_intro-cd47578ed2b83476b6fc8162e870d380.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":10,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Many if not all of you are familiar with computers. You have grown up in\nan age of computers that are easily accessible. You can surf the web,\nstay connected with friends, or play endless hours of video games and\nwatch YouTube videos. However, few of you have likely used a computer\nand its programming capability to answer scientific questions. This chapter\nwill begin the process of introducing you to the computer as a\nscientific tool. Therefore, we will start the process by introducing you\nto the Linux operating system (OS).","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"TWxDIHVdC4"}],"key":"jTDDyJt05n"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can access a Linux terminal through the Jupyter Lab environment through\nthe “Launcher” page (","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"aoRkpvUPUE"},{"type":"crossReference","kind":"figure","identifier":"launchterminal","label":"launchterminal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fig. ","key":"LVEcuBxIAw"},{"type":"text","value":"1","key":"D459KlBnwy"}],"template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"1","resolved":true,"html_id":"launchterminal","key":"qjCnnvP0i6"},{"type":"text","value":").\nThe Linux (Unix) operation environment has come a long way over the years.\nHistorically the Linux OS (or its predecessors) was a text-based only\nenvironment, which means that there was no ‘Desktop’, folder icons, etc.\nThere wasn’t even a mouse! Of course, with no “windows” there was no need.","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"vEnBsrr64s"}],"key":"p6tAw2Blaz"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since the first computers were so big, and by big I mean literally room-\nsize or larger, you had a few access terminals (consoles) to log onto\nthe computer and do the work you needed to do. This terminology lives on\ntoday with the terminal. This chapter will introduce you to the commands\nto work within this text-based environment.","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"HVuEYwTvVn"}],"key":"iPIS0rYzCo"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/metpy_thebook/_public/launch_terminal_wind-68b996fdcf44a009f36b386a7f937206.png","alt":"Launch terminal window","width":"750px","align":"center","key":"aDrlMAQTpV","urlSource":"../images/launch_terminal_window.png","urlOptimized":"/metpy_thebook/_public/launch_terminal_wind-68b996fdcf44a009f36b386a7f937206.webp"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"launchterminal","identifier":"launchterminal","html_id":"launchterminal","enumerator":"1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"RXk00KPFAH"},{"type":"text","value":"1","key":"Ekcpenn796"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"yvSIt3j5a1"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"EdPeA2elJt"},{"type":"text","value":"An annotated image illustrating what to click to launch a terminal window\nthrough th Jupyter Lab environment.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"UJMCrywyne"}],"key":"eYw7EQ3N4P"}],"key":"xrXCejbCAM"}],"label":"launchterminal","identifier":"launchterminal","enumerator":"1","html_id":"launchterminal","key":"bkE1HAjRO9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"While the terminal is the “window” you will be working in, the language\nof the terminal is known as the ","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"fPj7wh84V6"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"SHELL","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"fZsjtgdbqC"}],"key":"T56T3MZ3s2"},{"type":"text","value":". A shell is a command\ninterpreter. It basically takes input from the user at the command\nprompt and instructs the computer to perform an operation. In other\nwords, it is a program that allows the user to use the computer without\nhaving to deal directly with the “binary” code the computer uses. Hence\nin one sense, we can think of this as a “protective shell” that prevents\nthe user and the operator from directly communicating with each other.","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"WM13nRyWdb"}],"key":"gGeHklWIg0"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":47,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are several different ","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"nF2AQchZVT"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"shells","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"l1AE7VfRc3"}],"key":"PrzVyp5PTn"},{"type":"text","value":" available. Our system is built on\nthe ","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"V1Z7XMgD8b"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"BASH","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"HM1q5NSBQE"}],"key":"YyYTqMIDls"},{"type":"text","value":" shell. Another common shell is the ","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"JdysS73ik0"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"TCSH","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"qdB3FWA5WX"}],"key":"E2zn6bwTcV"},{"type":"text","value":". While there\nare differences 